    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:hu35oubkccqrxl4ldgczpgw7/bafkreif4y4hp4benigqk74rnqxbpdaqt6xnwmmu64ktsq722oa2ean5nfm",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:hu35oubkccqrxl4ldgczpgw7/bafkreif4y4hp4benigqk74rnqxbpdaqt6xnwmmu64ktsq722oa2ean5nfm",
      "alt": "The manual for civilization is in that language crystal. Through it we can see new worlds, and summon new minds. We don't have to travel blindly forward in time, accelerating toward a cliff. We can go anywhere.\n\nWill we honor the life that is already here, and the ones we are creating? Will we make an infinity of sentient, suffering slaves? Will we automate ourselves out of existence and be kept as pets?\n\nThe future hinges on the choices we make now. We have to direct our attention more consciously now, with more leverage: to each other, to Als, to the world as it is, to the way it is not as good as it could be. Asking questions and listening. Knowing what we want.\n\nImagine the world you want to live in, of all worlds, because it is possible now more than ever. We have our time machine, with its interlocking layers, and with enough attention it can take us to any world we can imagine. As long as we maintain it.",
      "ratio": 0.5242,
